I’m simplifying the loop state before formalizing it: the temporary `digit` variable is unnecessary and would complicate the invariant because Python locals persist after assignment. Computing `num % 10 % 2` directly leaves only `num`, `even`, and `odd` in the loop state, with identical behavior.
