I found a cleaner implementation that materially reduces the symbolic state space while preserving the contract: a decimal digit is even exactly when the current positive number is even. The loop can therefore add `1 - (num % 2)` to the even count and `num % 2` to the odd count, eliminating the inner branch. I’m updating both code and exact proof body to this equivalent arithmetic form.
