K does not use one untrusted target claim as a lemma for another target claim. I’m separating the independently proved loop theorem into its own spec module and importing that module into the whole-function spec. This is the sound modular pattern: the imported loop reachability theorem is the connection theorem for the loop summary, while its own module remains provable bridge-free.
